{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1500699-nagual-the-savage-fan-game-for-a-very-different-take-on-changing-breeds-for-2e","id":1500699,"title":"Nagual: The Savage (Fan-Game) for a very different take on Changing Breeds for 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-18T21:47:10-08:00","id":1500699,"title":"Nagual: The Savage (Fan-Game) for a very different take on Changing Breeds for 2e","content":"Hello! This is my first ever post on the Forums. <div align=\"center\"><b><i>Nagual: The Savage</i></b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is a game about Culture, Family, and Connections. Of Savagery, Civility, and Staying True. The Nagual are Shapeshifters bound together by the Rage of the Goddess of the Natural Cycles and Environmental Disasters. Her fury against the depredations of the unnatural against her beautiful lands. Not a game of Man vs Nature, but of Beast vs Monster. Of the Natural vs the Unnatural and how far you will go to do what is necessary to protect yourself, your land, and your family.<br /> <br /> The Core Rulebook for Nagual: the Savage is fully finished. The only thing that needs to be done for it is Editing and a bit of proofreading. I am now working on a Night Horrors Supplement. I have a Discord dedicated to the Splat, and if the above sounds interesting to you, and you want to know more about it, then by all means! Come join us! <a href=\"https://discord.gg/ZkX5px4x2H\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/ZkX5px4x2H</a><br /> <br /> Link to the Core Rulebook: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rYxBILf2PLVVKgF07shwMY6z9_lIcUEEEfne7iiTV44/edit%E2%80%8B\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rYxBILf2PLVVKgF07shwMY6z9_lIcUEEEfne7iiTV44/edit\u200b</a><br /> <br /> This began as a project to bring Werewolf the Apocalypse and its Fera to Chronicles of Darkness. However, there were a lot of things surrounding that property that I found particularly distasteful. So, that idea was abandoned. Instead, this is an entirely new take on Shapeshifters for the Chronicles of Darkness. With inspiration pulled from the original source. It also uses a few systems from other Game lines that I felt fit the aesthetic and theme I was going for.<br /> <br /> There are only Five Broods in this Core Rulebook with more if you want them to be found on my Discord Server. The Broods are Azeban the Raccoons, Bruin the Bears, Grimalkin the Cats, Gumo the Spiders, and Vargr the Wolves.<br /> <br /> They are seperated into three Breeds:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Glede the Nagual born. </b></i>These are the most common form of the Nagual, raised among their peers in Clans.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Scoria the Animal Born.</b></i> These are normal, Wild Cousins, of the Nagual Broods who are Called by Lurra-Ulaka after an encounter with the supernatural. The Nagual do not mate with animals.<br /> <br /> Finally, there are <i><b>Kindled, the Human Born.</b></i> These are humans who were Kindled into Nagual by another Nagual who felt they would fit in, or sought to use them. Mass Kindlers are a type of Wayward, a Nagual who has fallen from the grace of Lurra-Ulaka, called Lycanthropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","user":"Tonkers77","date":".  Added a lot of additional information, as Psychotobe said I should! 01-21-2023, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T19:57:44-08:00","id":1500804,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't it be better to provide a snippet of what you've made if you don't want the splat pdf openly available for whatever reason. Just so people can see how it's written. I imagine alot of people who would otherwise be interested may not enjoy joining a discord of a complete stranger","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27701-psychotobe","name":"Psychotobe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T01:08:34-08:00","id":1500822,"title":"","content":"Going to second that you might want to say a bit more so it doesn't come off as a way to get people onto your server.<br /> <br /> One thing specific to address is the concept of &quot;unnatural&quot; as the Chronicles of Darkness largely eschew the idea that supernatural or artificial are &quot;unnatural&quot; unless that's specifically part of a splat's core themes (Prometheans, Demons, and Deviants get this the most).<br /> <br /> It also feels like it's going to overlap a lot with some of the existing games. Werewolves and Beasts are notably very much into fighting under the aegis of an alien spiritual mother figure, with major themes around family and protecting you little piece of the world (the Uratha more literally with their territories, while the Begotten more esoterically with their astral Lairs). While I do think it's a good idea to focus on what your idea does rather than what it doesn't do, a more in depth pitch could help make it clear what makes your fan game's experience uniquely different from the other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T17:45:55-08:00","id":1500981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psychotobe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1500699-nagual-the-savage-fan-game-for-a-very-different-take-on-changing-breeds-for-2e?p=1500804#post1500804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it be better to provide a snippet of what you've made if you don't want the splat pdf openly available for whatever reason. Just so people can see how it's written. I imagine alot of people who would otherwise be interested may not enjoy joining a discord of a complete stranger</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good point! Like I said, first time using the Forums. I'll add the link to the Document!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T17:50:33-08:00","id":1500982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1500699-nagual-the-savage-fan-game-for-a-very-different-take-on-changing-breeds-for-2e?p=1500822#post1500822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to second that you might want to say a bit more so it doesn't come off as a way to get people onto your server.<br /> <br /> One thing specific to address is the concept of &quot;unnatural&quot; as the Chronicles of Darkness largely eschew the idea that supernatural or artificial are &quot;unnatural&quot; unless that's specifically part of a splat's core themes (Prometheans, Demons, and Deviants get this the most).<br /> <br /> It also feels like it's going to overlap a lot with some of the existing games. Werewolves and Beasts are notably very much into fighting under the aegis of an alien spiritual mother figure, with major themes around family and protecting you little piece of the world (the Uratha more literally with their territories, while the Begotten more esoterically with their astral Lairs). While I do think it's a good idea to focus on what your idea does rather than what it doesn't do, a more in depth pitch could help make it clear what makes your fan game's experience uniquely different from the other games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair! The Nagual are entirely focused upon the physical world. In their worldview, the &quot;natural&quot; is anything created by Lurra-Ulaka, so plants, animals, and normal, mundane humans. Things that do not derive power from elsewhere. They believe that when &quot;unnatural powers&quot; or things that derive their power from outside of Lurra's cycle, so pretty much everything else, begins to tamper with the natural such as Ghouling animals, or twisting the landscape with powers etc... this causes a problem and has fallout that the Nagual must deal with.<br /> <br /> It should be noted in the Core, this actually isn't focused upon the other Supernaturals. Instead, it's about Waywards, or Nagual who have fallen from their commandments given by Lurra. And their main antagonist, the Invasives. Pretty much horrific mutated monsters that come in a variety of flavors that warp the lands and animals around them to better feed. Much like Invasive Species.<br /> <br /> As far as overlap goes, yes. There is a little bit of overlap. I think any Splat about Shapeshifters is going to overlap with Werewolf regardless. So, instead of trying to twist it into not overlapping. I just focused on what part of those themes the Nagual tackles and keep them away from what Werewolf and Beast actually does. Werewolves with their focus upon the Shadow, and Beasts with their Astral Horrors and bringing in members of other Supernaturals. Nagual are kin to other Nagual, and their focus is on the material world and how other things interact with it nearly exclusively. Their family is found in their Broods, or other shifters of the same animal, their Clans which are usually blood relatives, and their Menageries, the other Nagual they work with to secure their territories. Where with Werewolf its about the Pack and the Shadow. Though, Packs can certainly be big enough to meet the standards of a Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","user":"Tonkers77","date":". 01-21-2023, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T04:15:52-08:00","id":1503013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__